- summary: |
    Implemented mim.Merge(base, user) (cut-1, single user module on top of
    standard MIM) and wired FOM-101 redefine detection into parser.Parse.
    Detection rules:
      - User dataType colliding with MIM dataType -> FOM-101.
      - MIM object class with user-added attributes -> FOM-101.
      - MIM interaction class with user-added parameters -> FOM-101.
      - Pass-through inheritance (HLAobjectRoot / HLAinteractionRoot used
        as roots with no attributes/parameters added) -> NOT FOM-101.
    parser/mim_merge.go skips MIM-typed modules to avoid self-collision on
    the embedded MIM itself.
    Refactored parser/datatype_ref.go to consume mim.StandardMIMHandle
    instead of the hardcoded mimPrimitives set; TODO(#1) marker removed.
